    "result_text": "There is only one test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented telephone normalization on owner creation (`POST /api/owners`). The change satisfies the spec \u2014 strip every non-digit character, require exactly 10 digits, store/return that 10-digit value, and reject with 400 otherwise.\n\nBecause the endpoint validates the request body with `@Valid @RequestBody` before any code runs, the DTO's telephone `pattern: '^[0-9]*$'` would have rejected an input like `(04) 1234-5678` at binding time \u2014 before it could ever be normalized. So the fix has two parts:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 removed the digits-only `pattern` from the `telephone` schema (keeping `minLength`/`maxLength`) so raw input reaches the pipeline. The generated `OwnerFieldsDto` is rebuilt without the `@Pattern` constraint.\n\n2. **`BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 after the required-field check, `normalizeTelephone` strips non-digits (`replaceAll(\"\\\\D\", \"\")`), throws the new checked `InvalidTelephoneException` when the result isn't exactly 10 digits, and writes the normalized value back onto the request before mapping to the `Owner` entity that gets saved and returned.\n\n3. **New 400 escalation** \u2014 `InvalidTelephoneException` + `InvalidTelephoneExceptionHandler` (returns a `ProblemDetail` with `HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST`), wired via `officefloor/escalation/\u2026InvalidTelephoneException.yml`, following the existing `MissingOwnerFieldsException` pattern.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (both `coreStripsToTenDigits` \u2192 `(04) 1234-5678` stored/returned as `0412345678`, and `errorRejectsTooFewDigits` \u2192 `12345` yields 400) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` build is **green**.",
